<title>ITALY: Italy bourse approves SanPaolo prospectus.</title>
<headline>Italy bourse approves SanPaolo prospectus.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian stock market watchdog Consob has given its approval to a prospectus for a public share offer by Turin-based bank San Paolo di Torino, a stock market commission source said.</p>
<p>San Paolo is set to go ahead on May 19 with a public sale offer (OPV) of 25 percent of the bank's stock after privately placing 20 percent with banks and financial institutions who will together form a core of stable shareholders.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
